{
  "_about": "Curated index of 108 fun animation concepts for the storyboard skill. Each entry maps a concept to (a) an owned engine preset when we have one (use it first - zero deps, render-safe, brand-colored): lottie_fetch.py prints ready-to-paste markup for it - the entry's \"markup\" when the preset needs host content (an SVG shape, a <canvas>, text, a sized box), else a <div> with its attrs/loop - and/or (b) a Lottie to fetch on demand via lottie_fetch.py. 55 concepts have no owned preset; no entry ships a direct Lottie URL (\"url\": null) - they carry a \"search\" term for LottieFiles & co: pick an animation, verify its license, then `lottie_fetch.py fetch <url> --out <project> --id <id>`. This is NOT a bundle of Lottie JSONs (licensing + bloat + dead-link risk); it's a taxonomy + fetch-on-use workflow. lottie_fetch.py records the source URL + date in <project>/assets/lottie/CREDITS.md.",
  "_count": 108,
  "_fields": {
    "id": "kebab id; also the local filename when fetched (<project>/assets/lottie/<id>.json)",
    "category": "grouping",
    "tags": "search keywords Claude matches against a beat's need",
    "preset": "storyboard-engine.js PRESETS name for data-anim (null = no owned preset: fetch a Lottie). Always a real preset, never a data-loop name",
    "loop": "optional data-loop (engine LOOPS: float|sway|breathe|rotate|orbit|pulse|shimmer|beat) to add on top of the preset. The loop starts when the entrance ends (t + dur), so a preset with an endless dur (9999: pulseRings, spinner, sparkle, ...) needs a finite data-dur in attrs or its loop never runs",
    "attrs": "optional extra attributes for the element (raw HTML attribute text), e.g. {\"data-fx\":\"rain\"} for emitter, {\"data-dur\":\"1\"} for an endless ambient preset",
    "markup": "optional complete snippet for presets that need host content or structure (donutSweep -> an SVG <circle>, constellation -> a <canvas>, codeType -> text, chartArea/lineDraw/connectorDraw/motionPath -> SVG, barGrow -> sized bars); lottie_fetch.py prints it instead of a bare <div>. It always contains data-anim=\"<preset>\"",
    "url": "direct Lottie JSON URL, or null when none is known - every entry carries the key: search-only entries (preset null) then have a \"search\" term; preset entries need no URL",
    "search": "suggested LottieFiles search term when fetching (present on search-only entries and as a richer alternative on some preset entries)",
    "license_note": "optional: what to check before shipping a fetched asset",
    "note": "optional usage hint printed by `lottie_fetch.py show`"
  },
  "_sources": {
    "lottiefiles_free": "https://lottiefiles.com/free — filter Free; many need attribution, some are personal-use only. Verify per asset.",
